   "source": [
    "### Q5: Construct a Phase I $R$ chart. Does the chart show evidence of statistical control? If not, identify the out-of-control subgroup(s) by number and provide a contextual explanation as to why these OOC points may have been observed, omit these points, and replot the chart until statistical control is observed."
   ]Iteration 1 (all 25 shifts): 
R = 0.1795, LCL = 0, UCL = 0.3795. Shift 19 is out of control (R = 0.6818 oz); no other range exceeds the UCL.
Iteration 2 (24 shifts, #19 removed): 
 R= 0.1586, UCL = 0.3353. All ranges fall inside the limits, so the R chart shows statistical control and the variability is stable. 24 subgroups are retained.
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "84ce15c7",
